message.content:
This description appears to come from a CBP ruling on a costume-type garment (a dress or robe with raw edges and loose stitching), likely a Halloween costume. Such garments are generally classified under 9505.90 as festive articles, but only if they are not well-made wearing apparel. Loose stitching and unfinished raw edges suggest a costume of flimsy construction, so heading 9505 fits (Note 1(e) to Chapter 95 excludes only well-made, durable apparel).

For 9505.90, the subheading covers other festive, carnival, or entertainment articles. Costumes fall under 9505.90.60 ("Other"), and the 10-digit statistical suffix is 9505.90.6000.

